  "steps": [
    "Put the chicken in a bowl with 1.5 tbsp olive oil, the smoked paprika, garlic powder, thyme, Aleppo pepper, cumin, cinnamon, salt, pepper, yogurt and lemon juice. Mix well, cover and refrigerate 2 to 10 hours (or cook right away if you are short on time).",
    "Take the chicken out of the fridge about 20 min before cooking to take the chill off.",
    "Make the salad: combine the onion, tomatoes and parsley, sprinkle with the salt and sumac, add the lemon juice and mix well. Let sit about 10 min, stirring a couple of times.",
    "Make the white sauce: mix the yogurt, mayonnaise, pickle juice, dill, salt and plenty of pepper. Taste and adjust.",
    "Heat a cast iron pan over medium heat with 1 tbsp oil. Cook the chicken in batches 4 min on the first side, flip and cook 4 min, then 1 to 2 min more on each side, 10 to 12 min total, until an instant-read thermometer reads at least 165°F.",
    "Add rice to each bowl, then chicken, then pile on the salad and sliced cucumbers. Scatter with herbs and drizzle with the white sauce."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "The yogurt and lemon in the marinade tenderize the chicken. About 50 g protein per bowl (creator's number).",
    "The creator serves it over low-carb rice. Any rice, cauliflower rice or quinoa works."
  ],
